{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00948",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.6,
      "end_seconds": 13.0,
      "duration_seconds": 10.4,
      "text": "G'day. Both my wrists are swollen and sore, and I can't say I've got much of an idea why."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.09,
      "end_seconds": 20.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Thanks for coming. When did the swelling begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.03,
      "end_seconds": 33.67,
      "duration_seconds": 9.64,
      "text": "Hard to say, mate. A while back. Couldn't tell you if it was the footy season or after."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.65,
      "end_seconds": 41.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "What's it like day to day? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.53,
      "end_seconds": 53.26,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "Sore in the morning, a bit better by lunch. I can still work. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.16,
      "end_seconds": 62.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Has anything made it better or worse? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.24,
      "end_seconds": 72.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Hot showers help. Typing on the laptop makes it worse. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.56,
      "end_seconds": 80.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "Tell me about your general health. Anything long-term?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.76,
      "end_seconds": 90.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.53,
      "text": "Psoriasis, on my elbows. Had it since I was a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.04,
      "end_seconds": 101.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.04,
      "text": "Interesting. That matters here. Does it flare when the joints are bad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.22,
      "end_seconds": 108.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Hard to say. Maybe a bit. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.37,
      "end_seconds": 128.28,
      "duration_seconds": 15.91,
      "text": "Let me explain what I think is going on. Joints are lined with a thin membrane. When it gets inflamed, it swells and hurts, and it's often worse in the morning. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.27,
      "end_seconds": 136.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Right. And that's what I've got? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.84,
      "end_seconds": 148.95,
      "duration_seconds": 9.11,
      "text": "It's what the pattern suggests, particularly with your psoriasis. I think this could be an inflammatory arthritis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.78,
      "end_seconds": 155.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Arthritis. At my age. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.72,
      "end_seconds": 166.7,
      "duration_seconds": 7.98,
      "text": "It can happen at any age, and it responds well to treatment. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.81,
      "end_seconds": 174.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "What do I do in the meantime? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.03,
      "end_seconds": 186.31,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "Wear a wrist splint at night, to rest the joints. You can buy one from the pharmacy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.24,
      "end_seconds": 192.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Will that help? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.03,
      "end_seconds": 204.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "It usually does. Also take regular breaks from typing, and stretch your wrists every hour."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.09,
      "end_seconds": 209.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "I can do that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.61,
      "end_seconds": 220.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.75,
      "text": "Heat, like your hot showers, is a good idea. Keep doing that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.25,
      "end_seconds": 226.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Good. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.84,
      "end_seconds": 233.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Is there anything you're worried about? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.9,
      "end_seconds": 243.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Just whether I'll still be able to work. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.88,
      "end_seconds": 252.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Most people carry on working, with some adjustments. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.44,
      "end_seconds": 258.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "That's a relief. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.12,
      "end_seconds": 269.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "Let me repeat the plan. Splints at night, breaks from typing, heat in the morning. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.33,
      "end_seconds": 274.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Got it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.4,
      "end_seconds": 285.81,
      "duration_seconds": 8.41,
      "text": "If the swelling isn't gone in two weeks, come back and see me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.29,
      "end_seconds": 292.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Two weeks. Righto. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.69,
      "end_seconds": 299.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Good. Take care. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.69,
      "end_seconds": 305.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. ~"
    }
  ]
}
